[?2004l=== CORRELATION SCRIPT BUG FIX SUMMARY ===

PROBLEM:
The correlate.py script was finding 80% fewer lateral movement candidates
than expected when analyzing Suricata eve.json logs.

ROOT CAUSE:
Two bugs in /home/user/correlate.py:

1. CRITICAL BUG (Line 22): Wrong event_type check
   - Script checked for: event_type == "netflow"
   - Suricata actually uses: event_type == "flow"
   - Result: ALL flow events were being skipped

2. SECONDARY BUG (Line 14): Incorrect timestamp format
   - Old format: "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S" (missing microseconds and timezone)
   - Correct format: "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.%f%z"
   - Suricata format: 2024-01-10T00:01:13.605445+0000

FIX APPLIED:
- Changed event_type check from "netflow" to "flow"
- Updated timestamp parsing to handle microseconds and timezone

VERIFICATION:
- Script now detects lateral movement candidate: 10.1.5.23
- This host connected to 90 distinct internal hosts (clear scanning behavior)
- Backup of original script saved as: /home/user/correlate.py.bak

